      <h2>About Spice Farm Tour (Kidichi)</h2>
      <div>Kidichi and Kizimbani spice farms offer immersive guided tours of Zanzibar's legendary spice plantations — cloves, nutmeg, cinnamon, vanilla, cardamom, black pepper, turmeric, and ginger grown in traditional agroforestry systems. Expert guides explain cultivation, harvesting, and the historical spice trade that made Zanzibar the 'Spice Island' and a global trade hub. Tours include tasting fresh spices, traditional hand-grinding demonstrations using mortar and pestle, and optional Swahili lunch featuring spice-infused dishes. The spice trade shaped Zanzibar's history, architecture, and multicultural identity.</div>
